{"repositoryId":1246939161,"availability":"available","full":"alyssom-fernandes/UnifyData-Python","name":"UnifyData-Python","description":"Month-end closing of employee purchases when Linx and HR share no code: fuzzy name matching with human review, payroll deduction sheet per company. Python + Streamlit, runs locally.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-22T18:12:51Z","updated":"2026-10-13T20:34:35Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://alyssom-fernandes.github.io/UnifyData-Web/?demo=1","topics":["dark-mode","data-cleaning","data-reconciliation","entity-resolution","excel","fuzzy-matching","name-matching","openpyxl","pandas","payroll","python","responsive","streamlit","thefuzz","xlsx"],"demo":"https://alyssom-fernandes.github.io/UnifyData-Web/?demo=1","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:47:44.896Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T02:47:44.896Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T02:47:44.896Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T02:47:44.896Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["UnifyData does the month-end closing of employee purchases for a group of companies. Employees buy on credit at the group's own stores, and Linx AutoSystem, the stores' management software, records each purchase. At the end of the month someone has to turn those Linx reports into a payroll deduction sheet for each company. When Linx and the HR spreadsheets share no common code, the only thing linking them is the name, and names are written in many ways: BAPTISTA in one place, BATISTA in the other; DEBORA without the accent; a surname cut short.","UnifyData matches people by name and asks a person only about what cannot be decided alone. Names that differ only by accent, case or spaces are linked automatically; similar names, repeated names and people who are not in HR become review cards; the result is the deduction sheet, one sheet per company."